            <p>An open-source project monitoring mosquito-borne diseases in Brazil.</p>
            <a class="text-link" href="https://info.dengue.mat.br/">
              Visit Infodengue <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
          </div>
          <div class="case-study-detail">
            <p class="eyebrow case-provenance">Past OSL collaboration · Team experience</p>
            <dl class="case-facts">
              <div>
                <dt>Project context</dt>
                <dd>A public-health monitoring platform using data and web tools
                  to make information on mosquito-borne diseases accessible.</dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt>What our team contributed</dt>
                <dd>Data visualization, development of the web platform,
                  and development and deployment infrastructure.</dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt>Public evidence</dt>
                <dd>
                  <a href="https://info.dengue.mat.br/">Project website <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
                  <a href="https://info.dengue.mat.br/informacoes/">Project information <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
                </dd>
              </div>
            </dl>
            <p class="case-context-note">
              This collaboration began at Open Science Labs; some contributors were later
              contracted directly by Infodengue. It is prior team experience, not a
              SciStitch client engagement.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="case-study-section section-pad" id="literev" aria-labelledby="literev-title">
        <div class="container section-grid">
          <div class="section-intro">
            <p class="eyebrow section-label"><span>03 /</span> Literature review</p>
            <h2 id="literev-title">LiteRev</h2>
            <p>A tool for finding and reviewing scientific literature, connected
              to The GRAPH Network and research at the University of Geneva.</p>
            <a class="text-link" href="https://literev.unige.ch/">
              Visit LiteRev <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
          </div>
          <div class="case-study-detail">
            <p class="eyebrow case-provenance">Past OSL collaboration · Team experience</p>
            <dl class="case-facts">
              <div>
                <dt>Project context</dt>
                <dd>Supporting the discovery and review of scientific literature
                  with research-oriented data processing and search workflows.</dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt>What our team contributed</dt>
                <dd>Technical leadership, AI, clustering, data processing,
                  benchmarking, Celery background tasks, Elasticsearch search,
                  web development, and DevOps.</dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt>Public evidence</dt>
                <dd>
                  <a href="https://literev.unige.ch/">Project website <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
                  <a href="https://thegraphnetwork.org/">The GRAPH Network <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
                </dd>
              </div>
            </dl>
            <p class="case-context-note">
              This work was carried out by a team formed at Open Science Labs.
              The case study describes that team's earlier contributions.
            </p>
          </div>
